course: dictionary
lesson: 10217
title: Tithe: a tenth for the church
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tithe is one tenth of something. Long ago, farmers gave a tithe of their harvest to the local church. «A real medieval village might owe rent to one lord, tithes (a tenth of its harvest) to a church and taxes to a king at the same time.» The brackets tell you what tithes means.
explain: Use the clues around the word. The sentence says the village owed tithes to a church, and the brackets say a tenth of its harvest. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A tenth of the crops fits, so a tithe is one tenth.
explain: Tithe can also be a verb: to tithe is to give a tenth. Some Christians today still tithe, giving a tenth of their income to their church. Farmers' tithes were often kept in a tithe barn, a big barn for storing grain.
fact: A tithe is one tenth, which is the same as ten per cent.
fact: «Tithes» means a tenth of a harvest or income, given to the church.
fact: A tithe barn was a big barn where farmers stored the grain they gave to the church.
fact: To tithe means to give a tenth of what you earn or grow.
fact: The idea of tithing comes from the Old Testament, a very old holy book.
exercise: «A real medieval village might owe tithes (a tenth of its harvest) to a church.» What is a tithe? | A kind of crop grown in fields | *One tenth of the harvest, given to the church | A tax paid to the king | A tall tower where the bells hang
exercise: A tithe barn was used to store what? | Horses and carts | *Grain that farmers gave to the church | Toys for the village children | Water for the fields
exercise: In maths, what is a tithe worth as a percentage? | 100 per cent | *10 per cent | 50 per cent | 1 per cent
test: «Long ago, farmers had to give a tithe of their crops to the local church.» What does tithe mean in this sentence? | *A tenth of their crops, given to the church | A bell in the church tower | A large bag of seeds | A fine paid to the lord
test: If a farmer had 100 sacks of grain, how many sacks would be a tithe? | 50 sacks | 100 sacks | 1 sack | *10 sacks
exam: «In the game, a village could owe rent to a lord, tithes to a church and taxes to a king all at once.» Which of these is a tithe? | *A tenth of the village's crops, given to the church | A tax paid to the king | A vague stretch of forest | A payment of rent to a lord
